{"name":"Ishtar","hex":"#484450","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Ishtar","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A goddess of fertility, love, sex, and war. In the Babylonian pantheon, she was the divine personification of the planet Venus; the Assyrian and Babylonian counterpart to the Sumerian Inanna and to the northwest-Semitic goddess Astarte."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Ishtar"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ishtar (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Ishtar is a 1987 American adventure comedy film written and directed by Elaine May, and produced by Warren Beatty, who co-stars opposite Dustin Hoffman. The story revolves around Chuck Clarke and Lyle Rogers, a duo of talentless American songwriters who travel to a booking in Morocco and stumble into a four-party Cold War standoff."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/58/Ishtar_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ishtar_(film)","wikidata":"Q2215067"},{"title":"Ishtar (singer)","blocks":[{"text":"Esther \"Eti\" Zach (Hebrew: אסתר \"אתי\" זך, known by her stage name Ishtar, is a French-Israeli vocalist best known for her work as the front vocalist of the French-based band Alabina, and her solo pop hits such as \"C'est la vie\", \"Last Kiss\", \"Horchat HaEkaliptus\" and \"Habibi \"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Ishtar%2C_briza_festival%2C_asqelon%27_2010.JPG/330px-Ishtar%2C_briza_festival%2C_asqelon%27_2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ishtar_(singer)","wikidata":"Q2048477"},{"title":"Inanna","blocks":[{"text":"Inanna is the ancient Mesopotamian goddess of war, love, and sex. She is also associated with political power, divine law, sensuality, and procreation. Originally worshipped in Sumer, she was known by the Akkadians, Babylonians, and Assyrians as Ishtar. Her primary title is \"the Queen of Heaven\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Ishtar_on_an_Akkadian_seal.jpg/330px-Ishtar_on_an_Akkadian_seal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inanna","wikidata":"Q272523"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Chaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png/500px-Chaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Chaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png/1280px-Chaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Chaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png/500px-Chaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chaos Monster and Sun God","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChaos_Monster_and_Sun_God.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Inanna_receiving_offerings_on_the_Uruk_Vase%2C_circa_3200-3000_BCE.jpg/500px-Inanna_receiving_offerings_on_the_Uruk_Vase%2C_circa_3200-3000_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Inanna_receiving_offerings_on_the_Uruk_Vase%2C_circa_3200-3000_BCE.jpg/1280px-Inanna_receiving_offerings_on_the_Uruk_Vase%2C_circa_3200-3000_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Inanna_receiving_offerings_on_the_Uruk_Vase%2C_circa_3200-3000_BCE.jpg/500px-Inanna_receiving_offerings_on_the_Uruk_Vase%2C_circa_3200-3000_BCE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Inanna receiving offerings on the Uruk Vase, circa 3200–3000 BCE","link":"https: